WEBVTT

00:16.495 --> 00:20.666
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

02:04.979 --> 02:07.273
Nice shot.
You're a chip off the old block.

02:07.857 --> 02:08.858
Guess so.

02:09.775 --> 02:10.776
Yumeka.

02:11.569 --> 02:12.570
Do you love basketball?

02:14.864 --> 02:16.114
Obviously!

02:16.115 --> 02:17.699
More than you love your dad?

02:17.700 --> 02:18.868
You're so annoying.

02:25.040 --> 02:28.544
Listen, Yumeka.
Make sure you cherish that feeling.

02:30.629 --> 02:32.173
This feeling called "love"

02:33.174 --> 02:35.801
is the most powerful feeling of all.

02:39.638 --> 02:41.973
So I guess you're the most powerful, too.

02:41.974 --> 02:43.808
You love Mom so much!

02:43.809 --> 02:47.354
That's right!
I love you and your Mom so much!

02:49.231 --> 02:50.608
I love you!

03:00.367 --> 03:01.785
Sorry for bothering you.

03:09.668 --> 03:11.587
KIKUCHI DENTAL CLINIC

03:12.171 --> 03:13.172
<i>I know already.</i>

03:14.548 --> 03:16.675
<i>That I'm blaming you.</i>

03:17.676 --> 03:21.513
<i>That I'm taking it out on you
because I quit basketball.</i>

03:27.144 --> 03:30.439
That one's still a first-year,
but she made the team.

03:30.981 --> 03:34.192
Apparently, she was pretty well-known
when she was in grade school.

03:34.193 --> 03:36.070
That's impressive.

03:36.570 --> 03:38.905
Although she doesn't look it.

03:38.906 --> 03:39.907
<i>Damn it!</i>

03:40.574 --> 03:44.161
<i>I didn't think it was going to be easy,
but I'm barely keeping up.</i>

03:45.037 --> 03:48.916
<i>I guess that makes sense since they have
one or two years of practice on me.</i>

03:57.466 --> 04:02.471
<i>I may have been talented in grade school,
but this is as far as it can take me.</i>

04:07.434 --> 04:08.560
Kido.

04:09.228 --> 04:11.313
I'm expecting good things from you
next time.

04:14.066 --> 04:15.067
Yes, sir.

04:15.651 --> 04:19.071
<i>That's right.
I just need to get better from this point.</i>

04:19.863 --> 04:22.825
<i>I just need to practice a ton like Natsu.</i>

04:23.492 --> 04:25.995
<i>I'm here because they expect me
to play well.</i>

04:26.745 --> 04:28.330
<i>I have to put in the work.</i>

04:32.835 --> 04:35.629
<i>Until I can taste blood.</i>

04:36.672 --> 04:39.091
<i>Until my hands are bone dry.</i>

04:47.516 --> 04:49.935
<i>Until my heart explodes
from beating so much.</i>

04:59.737 --> 05:02.489
<i>But all that gradually
started gnawing at me.</i>

05:04.616 --> 05:05.742
Think of your family!

05:05.743 --> 05:07.035
I'm home.

05:07.036 --> 05:08.411
This again?

05:08.412 --> 05:12.498
I understand that you're busy,
but I need you to listen to me.

05:12.499 --> 05:14.334
We talked about this
the other day already.

05:14.335 --> 05:17.837
You don't think about Yumeka or me at all!

05:17.838 --> 05:19.589
It's because you're like that...

05:19.590 --> 05:21.758
- So it's my fault?
- There you go again.

05:21.759 --> 05:23.426
How are you any different?

05:23.427 --> 05:26.429
I can't do this anymore.
Nothing I say gets through to you.

05:26.430 --> 05:27.681
That's not true.

05:33.187 --> 05:34.438
<i>But what can you do?</i>

05:35.481 --> 05:37.941
<i>Feelings change.</i>

05:42.029 --> 05:44.072
Did you change your nails?

05:44.073 --> 05:45.448
I did.

05:45.449 --> 05:46.450
Looks good, right?

05:47.493 --> 05:48.494
<i>Dad.</i>

05:49.411 --> 05:53.082
<i>I can feel myself gradually losing power.</i>

05:54.458 --> 05:56.585
<i>I'll be okay, though, right?</i>

05:57.169 --> 06:00.297
<i>The grueling practices are just
dragging me down right now,</i>

06:03.008 --> 06:06.720
<i>but my power
will eventually come back, right?</i>

06:15.771 --> 06:17.606
Good morning, Yumeka!

06:21.401 --> 06:22.986
You're here early as usual.

06:25.072 --> 06:26.198
Come practice with me.

06:33.956 --> 06:36.667
<i>I have to make sure
to hide this from Natsu.</i>

06:37.417 --> 06:42.256
<i>I don't want to influence her
with my negativity.</i>

06:48.595 --> 06:50.764
<i>Because she still loves basketball.</i>

06:52.891 --> 06:56.269
<i>In competition, you're not judged
by the time you put into practicing.</i>

06:56.270 --> 06:57.186
Rebound!

06:57.187 --> 06:58.104
Nice!

06:58.105 --> 06:59.231
Yumeka!

07:00.607 --> 07:05.028
<i>But the confidence you get from knowing
you did the hard work gives you strength.</i>

07:06.363 --> 07:07.573
<i>I have to.</i>

07:08.740 --> 07:10.659
<i>I have to score here.</i>

07:11.410 --> 07:13.036
<i>If I do, then I can still...</i>

07:15.914 --> 07:17.541
<i>But in the end,</i>

07:18.250 --> 07:19.376
<i>compared to her...</i>

07:46.028 --> 07:50.157
<i>Why didn't I practice more?</i>

07:52.534 --> 07:55.954
<i>Why didn't I take basketball
more seriously?</i>

07:59.041 --> 08:01.668
<i>Am I always going to feel like this?</i>

08:03.629 --> 08:06.381
<i>What was all my hard work
up until now for?</i>

08:09.635 --> 08:11.261
<i>This isn't fun.</i>

08:12.554 --> 08:14.473
<i>I'm tired.</i>

08:17.935 --> 08:20.812
<i>What am I even trying so hard for?</i>

08:40.082 --> 08:41.375
Yumeka.

08:43.544 --> 08:45.003
I need to talk to you.

08:46.463 --> 08:48.757
What? I'm trying to sleep.

08:51.176 --> 08:52.343
Listen.

08:52.344 --> 08:53.512
What already?

08:55.681 --> 08:58.767
Your father and I are getting divorced.

09:02.187 --> 09:04.856
So much for the most powerful feeling.

09:17.411 --> 09:18.453
<i>Help!</i>

09:24.835 --> 09:29.298
<i>I just wanted to play basketball
like I did back then.</i>

09:30.382 --> 09:34.803
<i>Back when I felt joy
for just getting the ball in the basket.</i>

09:39.057 --> 09:41.977
<i>I don't want to face the reality!</i>

09:58.660 --> 10:03.290
<i>I think... maybe... I don't love...</i>

10:05.167 --> 10:06.918
<i>basketball anymore...</i>

10:25.896 --> 10:27.314
<i>I was in pain.</i>

10:28.482 --> 10:31.942
<i>While I was becoming
more and more negative,</i>

10:31.943 --> 10:34.321
<i>Natsu kept charging forward.</i>

10:36.239 --> 10:37.324
<i>If only...</i>

10:38.659 --> 10:39.660
Yumeka!

10:41.828 --> 10:44.081
<i>If I stayed by Natsu's side,</i>

10:47.167 --> 10:48.377
<i>would I have</i>

10:49.419 --> 10:51.963
<i>fallen in love with basketball again?</i>

10:57.928 --> 10:59.011
What?

10:59.012 --> 11:03.100
This is a ticket to Chinatsu Senpai's
Winter Cup game.

11:04.434 --> 11:06.144
I'm giving it to you.

11:07.688 --> 11:10.649
This is a ticket to Chinatsu Senpai's
Winter Cup game.

11:11.358 --> 11:12.901
I'm giving it to you.

11:13.610 --> 11:15.904
So please go see...

11:16.530 --> 11:18.072
You're exhausted.

11:18.073 --> 11:19.908
My legs are at their limit.

11:20.742 --> 11:23.412
What do you mean you're giving it to me?

11:24.037 --> 11:25.747
Having someone like that in my life...

11:29.376 --> 11:31.420
Wouldn't it be better if you went?

11:32.254 --> 11:34.673
I know Natsu would be happier that way.

11:35.382 --> 11:36.800
It can't be me.

11:37.634 --> 11:39.428
It has to be you
when it comes to basketball.

11:41.888 --> 11:46.393
What's wrong with just going to see
an old friend's basketball game?

11:48.937 --> 11:52.356
Anyway, I went through a lot
to win this ticket,

11:52.357 --> 11:53.817
so please don't waste it!

11:56.403 --> 11:57.404
I'm counting on you.

12:09.791 --> 12:13.210
I can't believe
that first-year actually won.

12:13.211 --> 12:16.214
I bet Matsuoka is sore over it.

12:19.301 --> 12:22.721
Look how desperate you are.
Who are you giving the ticket to?

12:24.806 --> 12:28.726
Even if you don't tell me, I'll just ask
someone on the girl's team who came.

12:28.727 --> 12:29.728
That's unfair!

12:32.314 --> 12:34.064
It's Yumeka.

12:34.065 --> 12:35.734
Yumeka?

12:36.359 --> 12:38.486
She was on the basketball team
in junior high.

12:38.487 --> 12:39.988
No, I know that.

12:40.572 --> 12:42.281
Why bother at this point?

12:42.282 --> 12:43.365
What?

12:43.366 --> 12:44.743
She already quit.

12:45.327 --> 12:49.331
Someone like us getting involved
would just make Yumeka feel worse.

12:49.873 --> 12:52.501
It's not like she can come back to Eimei.

12:57.005 --> 12:58.006
That's true.

12:58.965 --> 13:01.551
I'm sure it's too late
for a lot of things.

13:02.594 --> 13:05.846
For Chinatsu Senpai,
Yumeka isn't just a part of her past.

13:05.847 --> 13:07.974
She's a part of her.

13:09.935 --> 13:11.686
<i>The Chinatsu Senpai I admire</i>

13:12.312 --> 13:15.190
<i>wouldn't be who she is without Yumeka.</i>

13:16.858 --> 13:19.819
I want them to be friends again.

13:22.822 --> 13:24.324
Call it my selfish desire.

13:29.496 --> 13:32.040
How was our first-year?

13:32.624 --> 13:36.419
I'm sure you could've kept going
if you didn't slip on your sweat.

13:37.754 --> 13:39.296
He didn't win by luck.

13:39.297 --> 13:40.924
What are you talking about?

13:41.508 --> 13:46.179
I'm sure you were already tired
from all the running you did this morning.

13:47.264 --> 13:50.307
I still challenged him to run
because I thought I could win.

13:50.308 --> 13:52.185
This was a measure of my ability too.

13:52.769 --> 13:55.187
That's a bad habit of yours.

13:55.188 --> 13:56.189
Is it?

13:56.773 --> 14:00.777
You might've gotten what you wanted
if you'd really put your all into it.

14:02.779 --> 14:05.240
I don't think it would have changed things
in this instance.

14:06.950 --> 14:08.410
That's true.

14:23.675 --> 14:24.676
I'm off, then.

14:41.192 --> 14:42.402
What happened?

14:43.945 --> 14:45.613
Chinatsu Senpai?

14:45.614 --> 14:47.781
What are you doing here?

14:47.782 --> 14:48.866
What about practice?

14:48.867 --> 14:51.286
Something came up!

14:51.870 --> 14:53.914
I promise I didn't skip.

14:54.873 --> 14:57.667
<i>I shouldn't tell her about Yumeka, right?</i>

15:06.051 --> 15:07.134
What was that for?

15:07.135 --> 15:09.930
If you don't wipe your sweat off,
you'll catch a cold again.

15:10.430 --> 15:12.181
But that's your towel.

15:12.182 --> 15:14.600
Don't worry, it's brand-new.

15:14.601 --> 15:16.102
I wasn't saying that for my sake.

15:19.522 --> 15:20.606
TAKE IT

15:20.607 --> 15:22.817
Could you stop making that face?

15:28.782 --> 15:30.825
Please wear that, too.

15:34.579 --> 15:36.330
Are you copying me?

15:36.331 --> 15:37.832
Not at all.

15:39.000 --> 15:41.752
You've given me so much over the year.

15:41.753 --> 15:43.588
I need to return the favor
from time to time.

15:48.635 --> 15:50.845
What are you going to give me next?

15:52.222 --> 15:53.348
Just kidding.

15:56.685 --> 16:00.105
I'm joking! Don't think too hard about it!

16:00.981 --> 16:03.024
<i>It's not like
she hasn't given me plenty already.</i>

16:03.608 --> 16:04.609
Then...

16:06.027 --> 16:08.154
whenever you're going through a hard time,

16:08.780 --> 16:10.115
I'll be by your side.

16:20.458 --> 16:22.460
Okay, no take-backs.

16:23.211 --> 16:25.630
I'm going to hold you to that.

16:27.549 --> 16:28.633
Go ahead.

16:30.385 --> 16:31.636
When that time comes,

16:32.429 --> 16:36.391
<i>it can be a concert, the beach,
or anywhere.</i>

16:37.017 --> 16:38.268
<i>I'll come with you.</i>

16:44.065 --> 16:46.026
WINTER CUP
GO FOR THE GOLD!

16:54.492 --> 16:57.244
How is it December 23rd already?

16:57.245 --> 16:59.371
You said the same thing
at the start of December.

16:59.372 --> 17:00.664
What do I do?

17:00.665 --> 17:03.834
The last time I didn't have a boyfriend
for Christmas was fifth grade!

17:03.835 --> 17:05.127
You were mature for your age.

17:05.128 --> 17:08.130
What are you so calm about?
You're single too.

17:08.131 --> 17:10.842
- Why aren't you panicking?
- There's no need to.

17:11.760 --> 17:14.095
I spend every year with my family.

17:15.096 --> 17:18.724
I have three siblings, so cooking
and getting ready is a lot of work.

17:18.725 --> 17:19.726
Three siblings?

17:20.310 --> 17:22.729
Last year, we even had
two different cakes.

17:26.024 --> 17:28.025
Why don't you spend yours
with family, too?

17:28.026 --> 17:31.988
My sister always has plans every year.

17:32.739 --> 17:34.615
She doesn't prioritize her family!

17:34.616 --> 17:35.700
Ayame!

17:37.160 --> 17:38.410
We were talking about

17:38.411 --> 17:41.205
going to karaoke after practice tomorrow.

17:41.206 --> 17:42.248
You should come.

17:43.041 --> 17:44.584
Hina!

17:45.585 --> 17:48.254
Nothing is more valuable
than having friends!

17:48.922 --> 17:50.756
Hina's musical is something else.

17:50.757 --> 17:52.008
What's that?

17:55.345 --> 17:58.223
Who cares about Christmas Eve, right?

18:00.850 --> 18:03.269
Come on, time to practice!

18:05.063 --> 18:07.023
You wanna come too, Taiki?

18:08.817 --> 18:11.277
We're all going to karaoke tomorrow.

18:15.865 --> 18:16.866
Sorry.

18:17.367 --> 18:20.286
I promised Nishida Senpai
I'd join him for extra practice.

18:20.912 --> 18:23.498
He said it would be
an all-guys Strength Training Eve.

18:24.874 --> 18:25.959
I see.

18:26.835 --> 18:30.254
Well, how about we forget this gym freak
and go have fun!

18:30.255 --> 18:31.964
Sounds good!

18:31.965 --> 18:33.924
Are you a good singer?

18:33.925 --> 18:36.552
When Hina starts singing,
you'll be able to see the stage.

18:36.553 --> 18:38.555
Niina, stop exaggerating.

18:39.139 --> 18:40.681
Well, see you tomorrow.

18:40.682 --> 18:41.891
See you tomorrow.

18:43.101 --> 18:47.855
Let's stay focused
for tomorrow's Winter Cup!

18:47.856 --> 18:49.022
Yeah!

18:49.023 --> 18:50.899
Don't let the cold get you!

18:50.900 --> 18:51.984
Yeah!

18:51.985 --> 18:53.944
Get fired up for this win!

18:53.945 --> 18:55.028
Yeah!

18:55.029 --> 18:57.197
Go, Eimei!

18:57.198 --> 18:58.782
Yeah!

18:58.783 --> 19:01.118
I guess the girls' basketball team
has a game tomorrow.

19:01.119 --> 19:02.244
What time does it start?

19:02.245 --> 19:03.745
Maybe 1:00 p.m.?

19:03.746 --> 19:05.206
Good luck, you guys!

19:05.915 --> 19:07.041
Thanks!

19:09.043 --> 19:10.794
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

19:10.795 --> 19:12.213
Thanks.

19:26.311 --> 19:28.353
So, are you okay to meet up
at 1:00 p.m. tomorrow?

19:28.354 --> 19:29.355
What?

19:29.939 --> 19:31.440
For our Christmas date.

19:31.441 --> 19:34.026
We'll go buy gifts for each other,

19:34.027 --> 19:36.069
head to a cafe with good coffee,

19:36.070 --> 19:38.155
then check out some Christmas lights.

19:38.156 --> 19:39.406
I thought we could go here...

19:39.407 --> 19:40.949
Hey, Sosuke.

19:40.950 --> 19:44.453
And if possible,
I'd like you to wear knee-high socks.

19:44.454 --> 19:46.497
I'm joking.

19:47.123 --> 19:48.999
I'm going to the bathroom.

19:49.000 --> 19:50.001
Okay.

20:01.346 --> 20:03.264
- That's...
- What is this?

20:03.973 --> 20:07.018
A ticket for a high school
basketball game tomorrow?

20:07.936 --> 20:09.102
You should go to this!

20:09.103 --> 20:11.355
The girl from the other day
is playing, right?

20:11.356 --> 20:15.026
Don't worry about me.
We can go on our date after the game.

20:16.236 --> 20:18.278
Why are you standing there? Sit down.

20:18.279 --> 20:19.280
Okay.

20:20.406 --> 20:25.036
What did you want to be when you grew up
back in elementary school?

20:27.038 --> 20:28.039
DREAM
BASKETBALL PLAYER

20:28.790 --> 20:30.290
I wanted to be a soccer player.

20:30.291 --> 20:31.833
I didn't know that.

20:31.834 --> 20:34.045
I totally forgot about it, too.

20:34.629 --> 20:38.132
It wasn't that I gave up on it,
it just kind of faded.

20:39.384 --> 20:41.385
But in your case, it looks to me

20:41.386 --> 20:44.555
that you used to have
a clear goal in mind,

20:45.265 --> 20:48.643
<i>which is why you're hesitating
about what to do now.</i>

20:51.646 --> 20:53.064
I mean,

20:53.731 --> 20:57.067
when that happens,
you need to strip away the chaff.

20:57.068 --> 20:58.151
Strip away?

20:58.152 --> 20:59.236
PATHETIC
NO APPRECIATION

20:59.237 --> 21:04.534
<i>In life, negative things
start sticking to the fun stuff.</i>

21:07.412 --> 21:10.038
<i>If you strip off each of them one by one</i>

21:10.039 --> 21:11.249
<i>and look at the core,</i>

21:13.251 --> 21:16.254
I bet you'll find
that you still love basketball.

21:18.172 --> 21:20.799
HATE

21:20.800 --> 21:22.593
LOVE

21:26.556 --> 21:30.101
Your obsession might not be
such a bad thing after all.

21:33.187 --> 21:34.856
There it is.

21:35.440 --> 21:39.901
You tend to mess with your bangs
when you try to hide your feelings.

21:39.902 --> 21:41.612
- What?
- You didn't know?

21:43.531 --> 21:45.158
<i>It's nothing but hard work.</i>

21:46.451 --> 21:49.620
<i>But there are people
who handle it with ease.</i>

21:50.705 --> 21:51.706
<i>It's okay if you quit.</i>

21:52.623 --> 21:54.125
<i>There's no need to push yourself.</i>

22:04.469 --> 22:05.470
<i>But...</i>

22:06.596 --> 22:08.389
<i>don't forget that excitement.</i>

22:09.474 --> 22:11.142
<i>Be confident in what you love.</i>

22:15.646 --> 22:16.898
<i>Because this feeling...</i>

22:18.358 --> 22:19.942
<i>will make you the most powerful.</i>

22:20.985 --> 22:23.905
EPISODE 29
LOVE IS THE MOST POWERFUL FEELING

23:48.865 --> 23:53.870
Subtitle translation by: Zensho Yamamoto
